":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"ecea6a5b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:34.821519Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:34.820968Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.041771Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.040826Z"},"id":"ecea6a5b","outputId":"248ebf5d-374c-4fbe-b2fe-d0045181cd21"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 1300x400 with 3 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 4 — Respuesta\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(13, 4))\n","\n","axes[0].boxplot(df['height'])\n","axes[0].set_title('Boxplot: height')\n","\n","axes[1].boxplot(df['weight'])\n","axes[1].set_title('Boxplot: weight')\n","\n","axes[2].hist(df['height'], bins=8, edgecolor='black')\n","axes[2].set_title('Histograma: height')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"67761a48","metadata":{"id":"67761a48"},"source":["### Ejercicio 5\n","Calcular la covarianza y la correlación de Pearson entre `height` y `weight`. Verificar que `corr = cov / (std_x * std_y)`. Graficar el scatter distinguiendo por `gender`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"096114db","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.043889Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.043256Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.158834Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.157817Z"},"id":"096114db","outputId":"686f8a91-c841-4917-ab22-d34fef43dba5"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Covarianza          = 61.7907\n","Correlación (Pandas) = 0.6642\n","Correlación (manual) = 0.6642\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 5 — Respuesta\n","cov_hw = df['height'].cov(df['weight'])\n","corr_hw = df['height'].corr(df['weight'])\n","corr_manual = cov_hw / (df['height'].std() * df['weight'].std())\n","\n","print(f\"Covarianza          = {cov_hw:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Correlación (Pandas) = {corr_hw:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Correlación (manual) = {corr_manual:.4f}\")\n","\n","base = df[df.gender == 'M'].plot.scatter(x='weight', y='height', color='blue', marker='o', s=25, label='M')\n","df[df.gender == 'F'].plot.scatter(x='weight', y='height', color='red', marker='o', s=25, ax=base, label='F')\n","plt.title('Height vs Weight por género')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0b71dfb4","metadata":{"id":"0b71dfb4"},"source":["## Apartado 2 · Distribuciones de probabilidad y cuantiles (Ejercicios 6–10)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e1ed1d48","metadata":{"id":"e1ed1d48"},"source":["### Ejercicio 6\n","Calcular los cuantiles de la Normal estándar (μ=0, σ=1) para α = 0.95 y α = 0.975 (útiles para IC de 90% y 95%)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"6ea94295","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.160348Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.160206Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.164790Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.164093Z"},"id":"6ea94295","outputId":"508637bd-57f2-4c69-e16b-3865fc2ae547"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["z(0.95)  = 1.6449\n","z(0.975) = 1.9600\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 6 — Respuesta\n","mu, sigma = 0, 1\n","q95 = st.norm.ppf(0.95, loc=mu, scale=sigma)\n","q975 = st.norm.ppf(0.975, loc=mu, scale=sigma)\n","print(f\"z(0.95)  = {q95:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"z(0.975) = {q975:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"74393fae","metadata":{"id":"74393fae"},"source":["### Ejercicio 7\n","Calcular los cuantiles de la distribución t-Student para α = 0.95 y α = 0.975, variando los grados de libertad, y verificar que convergen a los valores de la Normal cuando `df` es muy grande."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"955b08a0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.166491Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.166001Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.171189Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.170526Z"},"id":"955b08a0","outputId":"4ae2349d-fc94-458e-9156-625a3e69d2e5"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["--- alpha = 0.95 ---\n","  df =      10  ->  t = 1.812461\n","  df =      50  ->  t = 1.675905\n","  df =     100  ->  t = 1.660234\n","  df =    2000  ->  t = 1.645616\n","  df =  100000  ->  t = 1.644869\n","  Normal equivalente -> z = 1.644854\n","\n","--- alpha = 0.975 ---\n","  df =      10  ->  t = 2.228139\n","  df =      50  ->  t = 2.008559\n","  df =     100  ->  t = 1.983972\n","  df =    2000  ->  t = 1.961151\n","  df =  100000  ->  t = 1.959988\n","  Normal equivalente -> z = 1.959964\n","\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 7 — Respuesta\n","for alpha in [0.95, 0.975]:\n","    print(f\"--- alpha = {alpha} ---\")\n","    for dof in [10, 50, 100, 2000, 100000]:\n","        val = st.t.ppf(alpha, dof)\n","        print(f\"  df = {dof:7d}  ->  t = {val:.6f}\")\n","    print(f\"  Normal equivalente -> z = {st.norm.ppf(alpha):.6f}\\n\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e73d5224","metadata":{"id":"e73d5224"},"source":["### Ejercicio 8\n","Calcular P(X ≤ 8) para una Chi-cuadrado con 5 grados de libertad, y luego el cuantil correspondiente a esa probabilidad, verificando que el cuantil es la función inversa de la CDF."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"804b0577","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.172808Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.172301Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.176814Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.176005Z"},"id":"804b0577","outputId":"3862685c-cca4-4be8-c653-44c251eb275a"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["P(X<=8) con df=5 = 0.843764\n","Cuantil(alpha=0.843764, df=5) = 8.000000  (debe ser ~8)\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 8 — Respuesta\n","dof = 5\n","p = st.chi2.cdf(8, dof)\n","q = st.chi2.ppf(p, dof)\n","print(f\"P(X<=8) con df=5 = {p:.6f}\")\n","print(f\"Cuantil(alpha={p:.6f}, df=5) = {q:.6f}  (debe ser ~8)\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"640fcca6","metadata":{"id":"640fcca6"},"source":["### Ejercicio 9\n","Simular 1000 observaciones N(μ=5, σ=2), graficar su histograma normalizado junto con la densidad teórica (pdf) de la Normal, y calcular la media y varianza muestrales."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"c9fa1349","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.178978Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.178300Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.272768Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.271999Z"},"id":"c9fa1349","outputId":"6932aab3-1233-4360-a4df-c65055c3a05b"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Media muestral    = 5.0387  (teórica = 5)\n","Varianza muestral = 3.8355  (teórica = 4)\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 9 — Respuesta\n","np.random.seed(42)\n","mu_sim, sigma_sim = 5, 2\n","x = np.random.randn(1000) * sigma_sim + mu_sim\n","\n","plt.hist(x, bins=30, density=True, alpha=0.6, edgecolor='black', label='Muestra')\n","grid = np.linspace(x.min(), x.max(), 200)\n","plt.plot(grid, st.norm.pdf(grid, mu_sim, sigma_sim), 'r-', lw=2, label='pdf teórica')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.title('Histograma vs. densidad Normal teórica')\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(f\"Media muestral    = {x.mean():.4f}  (teórica = {mu_sim})\")\n","print(f\"Varianza muestral = {x.var(ddof=1):.4f}  (teórica = {sigma_sim**2})\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b300615f","metadata":{"id":"b300615f"},"source":["### Ejercicio 10\n","Graficar la densidad (pdf) de la distribución F para distintas combinaciones de grados de libertad (dfn, dfd), mostrando cómo cambia la forma de la curva."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"2258135f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.274508Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.274006Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.362606Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.361751Z"},"id":"2258135f","outputId":"a5e5ff9c-260b-4e45-af4a-29902c807cf4"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 10 — Respuesta\n","grid = np.linspace(0.01, 5, 300)\n","combos = [(5, 5), (10, 10), (20, 30), (5, 30)]\n","\n","for dfn, dfd in combos:\n","    plt.plot(grid, st.f.pdf(grid, dfn, dfd), label=f'dfn={dfn}, dfd={dfd}')\n","\n","plt.title('Densidad de la distribución F para distintos grados de libertad')\n","plt.xlabel('x')\n","plt.ylabel('pdf')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1ef8e428","metadata":{"id":"1ef8e428"},"source":["## Apartado 3 · Estimación por intervalos de confianza (Ejercicios 11–15)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2275edcf","metadata":{"id":"2275edcf"},"source":["### Ejercicio 11\n","Usando la variable `height` del dataset de estudiantes, calcular el Error Estándar de la Media (SEM) y el Intervalo de Confianza del 90% usando (a) el cuantil aproximado de la Normal estándar, (b) el cuantil exacto de la Normal, y (c) el cuantil exacto de la t-Student."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"04feffa3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.364616Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.364070Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.370297Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.369494Z"},"id":"04feffa3","outputId":"d5fcc436-be5a-48d0-c65b-f954cd649f0c"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["SEM = 1.9038,  media = 170.0353\n","IC90% (aprox. Normal) = (np.float64(166.90346812334158), np.float64(173.16712011195247))\n","IC90% (exacto Normal) = (np.float64(166.9037467950244), np.float64(173.16684144026965))\n","IC90% (exacto t-Student) = (np.float64(166.71140118123637), np.float64(173.35918705405766))\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 11 — Respuesta\n","x = df['height'].values\n","n = len(x)\n","x_mean = x.mean()\n","SEM = x.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(n)\n","\n","ic_a = (x_mean - 1.645 * SEM, x_mean + 1.645 * SEM)\n","ic_b = (x_mean - st.norm.ppf(0.95) * SEM, x_mean + st.norm.ppf(0.95) * SEM)\n","ic_c = st.t.interval(0.90, df=n - 1, loc=x_mean, scale=SEM)\n","\n","print(f\"SEM = {SEM:.4f},  media = {x_mean:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"IC90% (aprox. Normal) = {ic_a}\")\n","print(f\"IC90% (exacto Normal) = {ic_b}\")\n","print(f\"IC90% (exacto t-Student) = {ic_c}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c294d66d","metadata":{"id":"c294d66d"},"source":["### Ejercicio 12\n","Repetir el cálculo anterior para los niveles de confianza 95% y 99%, comparando en una tabla los resultados de la Normal vs. la t-Student."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"0aa92836","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.371753Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.371572Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.381222Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.380459Z"},"id":"0aa92836","outputId":"ec81670c-7cf0-410b-b4a3-5c1938629e85"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>IC_Normal_low</th>\n","      <th>IC_Normal_high</th>\n","      <th>IC_t_low</th>\n","      <th>IC_t_high</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>nivel</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0.95</th>\n","      <td>166.303825</td>\n","      <td>173.766763</td>\n","      <td>165.999322</td>\n","      <td>174.071266</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0.99</th>\n","      <td>165.131313</td>\n","      <td>174.939275</td>\n","      <td>164.474577</td>\n","      <td>175.596011</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["       IC_Normal_low  IC_Normal_high    IC_t_low   IC_t_high\n","nivel                                                       \n","0.95      166.303825      173.766763  165.999322  174.071266\n","0.99      165.131313      174.939275  164.474577  175.596011"]},"execution_count":14,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 12 — Respuesta\n","niveles = [0.95, 0.99]\n","resultados = []\n","for nivel in niveles:\n","    ic_norm = st.norm.interval(nivel, loc=x_mean, scale=SEM)\n","    ic_t = st.t.interval(nivel, df=n - 1, loc=x_mean, scale=SEM)\n","    resultados.append({\n","        'nivel': nivel,\n","        'IC_Normal_low': ic_norm[0], 'IC_Normal_high': ic_norm[1],\n","        'IC_t_low': ic_t[0], 'IC_t_high': ic_t[1]\n","    })\n","\n","tabla_ic = pd.DataFrame(resultados).set_index('nivel')\n","tabla_ic\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"57ffe25f","metadata":{"id":"57ffe25f"},"source":["### Ejercicio 13\n","Calcular el Intervalo de Confianza del 95% para una proporción en dos escenarios: (a) 55 de 100 encuestados responden positivamente, (b) 550 de 1000. Interpretar si el candidato puede estar seguro de superar el 50%."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"a7a576fc","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.382635Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.382494Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.387867Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.387119Z"},"id":"a7a576fc","outputId":"5845077d-7f72-4d3b-d49e-9118a9d1f34b"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["n=  100  p_hat=0.550  IC95%=(np.float64(0.4525), np.float64(0.6475))  ¿Supera 50% con seguridad? NO\n","n= 1000  p_hat=0.550  IC95%=(np.float64(0.5192), np.float64(0.5808))  ¿Supera 50% con seguridad? SÍ\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 13 — Respuesta\n","def ic_proporcion(n_yes, n_total, nivel=0.95):\n","    p_hat = n_yes / n_total\n","    SE = np.sqrt(p_hat * (1 - p_hat) / n_total)\n","    return p_hat, st.norm.interval(nivel, loc=p_hat, scale=SE)\n","\n","for n_yes, n_total in [(55, 100), (550, 1000)]:\n","    p_hat, ic = ic_proporcion(n_yes, n_total)\n","    seguro = \"SÍ\" if ic[0] > 0.5 else \"NO\"\n","    print(f\"n={n_total:5d}  p_hat={p_hat:.3f}  IC95%={tuple(round(v,4) for v in ic)}  ¿Supera 50% con seguridad? {seguro}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ba7d07af","metadata":{"id":"ba7d07af"},"source":["### Ejercicio 14\n","Usando `height` y `weight`, calcular el coeficiente de correlación de Pearson y su Intervalo de Confianza del 95% y 99% aplicando la transformación z de Fisher."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"098fc7f1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.389634Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.389090Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.395180Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.394469Z"},"id":"098fc7f1","outputId":"3d269d2e-ee96-4a0c-d718-bc576d033d8b"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["r = 0.6642\n","IC95% = {'low': np.float64(0.26960396330592223), 'high': np.float64(0.8677953581441814)}\n","IC99% = {'low': np.float64(0.11137578298592947), 'high': np.float64(0.9030812794020874)}\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 14 — Respuesta\n","x_h = df['height']\n","y_w = df['weight']\n","n2 = len(x_h)\n","r = x_h.corr(y_w)\n","z = np.arctanh(r)\n","se_z = 1 / np.sqrt(n2 - 3)\n","\n","ic95 = {'low': np.tanh(z - st.norm.ppf(0.975) * se_z), 'high': np.tanh(z + st.norm.ppf(0.975) * se_z)}\n","ic99 = {'low': np.tanh(z - st.norm.ppf(0.995) * se_z), 'high': np.tanh(z + st.norm.ppf(0.995) * se_z)}\n","\n","print(f\"r = {r:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"IC95% = {ic95}\")\n","print(f\"IC99% = {ic99}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b0b5f90d","metadata":{"id":"b0b5f90d"},"source":["### Ejercicio 15\n","Construir un Intervalo de Confianza del 95% para la media de `weight` mediante **bootstrap** (remuestreo con reemplazo, 5000 réplicas) y comparar contra el IC paramétrico basado en la t-Student."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"5639a22e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.396582Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.396443Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.532633Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.531864Z"},"id":"5639a22e","outputId":"35f83cbd-7aa8-40c5-ca62-d7cb908434a9"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Media muestral = 61.0647\n","IC95% Bootstrap    = (np.float64(55.87602941176471), np.float64(66.63573529411765))\n","IC95% Paramétrico  = (np.float64(54.97113197338879), np.float64(67.15827979131709))\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 15 — Respuesta\n","np.random.seed(1)\n","w = df['weight'].values\n","n_w = len(w)\n","B = 5000\n","\n","boot_means = np.array([w[np.random.randint(0, n_w, n_w)].mean() for _ in range(B)])\n","ic_boot = (np.percentile(boot_means, 2.5), np.percentile(boot_means, 97.5))\n","\n","w_mean = w.mean()\n","sem_w = w.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(n_w)\n","ic_param = st.t.interval(0.95, df=n_w - 1, loc=w_mean, scale=sem_w)\n","\n","print(f\"Media muestral = {w_mean:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"IC95% Bootstrap    = {ic_boot}\")\n","print(f\"IC95% Paramétrico  = {ic_param}\")\n","\n","plt.hist(boot_means, bins=40, edgecolor='black')\n","plt.axvline(ic_boot[0], color='red', ls='--')\n","plt.axvline(ic_boot[1], color='red', ls='--')\n","plt.title('Distribución bootstrap de la media (weight)')\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"14a9313c","metadata":{"id":"14a9313c"},"source":["## Apartado 4 · Pruebas de hipótesis (Ejercicios 16–20)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"786f83b5","metadata":{"id":"786f83b5"},"source":["### Ejercicio 16\n","Simular una muestra Normal (n=10, μ=3, σ=2) y realizar un test t de una muestra (`ttest_1samp`) contra μ₀=0, comparando con el cálculo manual del estadístico t y su p-valor a dos colas."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"070e6b14","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.534252Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.534100Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.540503Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.539801Z"},"id":"070e6b14","outputId":"e0210dbc-90f3-414d-8bfa-d89af9d66e9e"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["SciPy  ttest_1samp: TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(3.8682023385794677), pvalue=np.float64(0.0037991794351627237), df=np.int64(9))\n","Manual: t = 3.8682, p-valor (2 colas) = 0.0038\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 16 — Respuesta\n","np.random.seed(1234)\n","n1s = 10\n","mu_true, sigma_true = 3, 2\n","x1s = np.random.randn(n1s) * sigma_true + mu_true\n","\n","mu_0 = 0\n","res_scipy = st.ttest_1samp(x1s, mu_0)\n","\n","x_mean1 = x1s.mean()\n","SEM1 = x1s.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(n1s)\n","t_manual = (x_mean1 - mu_0) / SEM1\n","p_manual = 2 * st.t.sf(np.abs(t_manual), df=n1s - 1)\n","\n","print(\"SciPy  ttest_1samp:\", res_scipy)\n","print(f\"Manual: t = {t_manual:.4f}, p-valor (2 colas) = {p_manual:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9218ef96","metadata":{"id":"9218ef96"},"source":["### Ejercicio 17\n","Simular dos muestras independientes (n1=10, μ1=3, σ1=2) y (n2=20, μ2=5, σ2=3) y realizar un test t de dos muestras independientes asumiendo varianzas distintas (Welch), tanto con los datos crudos como con `ttest_ind_from_stats`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"39a39c93","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.541961Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.541816Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.547482Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.546811Z"},"id":"39a39c93","outputId":"dfe32de2-6c91-4f25-aa9b-4435f08edd50"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Test directo : TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-2.870701133767877), pvalue=np.float64(0.009090146778647536), df=np.float64(21.218504456666945))\n","Test desde stats: Ttest_indResult(statistic=np.float64(-2.870701133767877), pvalue=np.float64(0.009090146778647536))\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 17 — Respuesta\n","n1, n2 = 10, 20\n","mu1, mu2 = 3, 5\n","sigma1, sigma2 = 2, 3\n","x1 = np.random.randn(n1) * sigma1 + mu1\n","x2 = np.random.randn(n2) * sigma2 + mu2\n","\n","res_directo = st.ttest_ind(x1, x2, equal_var=False)\n","\n","x1_mean, x2_mean = x1.mean(), x2.mean()\n","s1, s2 = x1.std(ddof=1), x2.std(ddof=1)\n","res_from_stats = st.ttest_ind_from_stats(x1_mean, s1, n1, x2_mean, s2, n2, equal_var=False)\n","\n","print(\"Test directo :\", res_directo)\n","print(\"Test desde stats:\", res_from_stats)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4f77465c","metadata":{"id":"4f77465c"},"source":["### Ejercicio 18\n","Simular un diseño de muestras pareadas (x2 = x1 + ruido) y comparar el resultado del test t pareado (`ttest_rel`) contra el test t independiente sobre el mismo par de muestras, evidenciando la diferencia de potencia estadística."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"374ec98a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.548938Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.548718Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.554962Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.554163Z"},"id":"374ec98a","outputId":"62274888-588b-4bd7-9ed8-4a228783d2fb"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Test pareado    : TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-3.2467018903823366), pvalue=np.float64(0.010050268032570107), df=np.int64(9))\n","Test independiente: TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.523719559914853), pvalue=np.float64(0.6069034633660739), df=np.float64(17.88383285037342))\n","\n","El p-valor difiere notablemente: el diseño pareado controla la variabilidad individual.\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 18 — Respuesta\n","n_p = 10\n","x1p = np.random.randn(n_p) * 5 + 3\n","x2p = x1p + np.random.randn(n_p) * 1 + 1\n","\n","res_pareado = st.ttest_rel(x1p, x2p)\n","res_independiente = st.ttest_ind(x1p, x2p, equal_var=False)\n","\n","print(\"Test pareado    :\", res_pareado)\n","print(\"Test independiente:\", res_independiente)\n","print(\"\\nEl p-valor difiere notablemente: el diseño pareado controla la variabilidad individual.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"10588c21","metadata":{"id":"10588c21"},"source":["### Ejercicio 19\n","Con los puntajes de tres grupos de estudiantes, ejecutar un ANOVA de un factor (`f_oneway`) para determinar si existen diferencias significativas entre las medias de los grupos."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"924a6539","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.556891Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.556279Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.562476Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.561583Z"},"id":"924a6539","outputId":"bdc54480-d200-4e25-92ec-36f55dc88d43"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Estadístico F = 0.2837\n","p-valor       = 0.7563\n","No se rechaza H0: no hay evidencia de diferencia significativa.\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 19 — Respuesta\n","g1 = np.array([82, 93, 61, 74, 69, 70, 53])\n","g2 = np.array([71, 62, 85, 94, 78, 66, 71])\n","g3 = np.array([64, 73, 87, 91, 56, 78, 87])\n","\n","res_anova = st.f_oneway(g1, g2, g3)\n","print(f\"Estadístico F = {res_anova.statistic:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"p-valor       = {res_anova.pvalue:.4f}\")\n","\n","alpha = 0.05\n","conclusion = \"Se rechaza H0: hay diferencia significativa entre grupos.\" if res_anova.pvalue < alpha \\\n","    else \"No se rechaza H0: no hay evidencia de diferencia significativa.\"\n","print(conclusion)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fee94b4f","metadata":{"id":"fee94b4f"},"source":["### Ejercicio 20\n","Realizar (a) un test Chi-cuadrado de varianza para una muestra simulada (H0: σ²=σ₀²) y (b) un test F de razón de varianzas entre dos muestras con distinta dispersión, reportando estadístico y p-valor en ambos casos."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"5014b2f2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.564007Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.563846Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.571441Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.570691Z"},"id":"5014b2f2","outputId":"c9bd8618-c0c4-4a07-b672-cc966231e4e8"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["(a) Chi2 test: estadístico=23.0676, p-valor (2 colas)=0.4688"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","(b) F test: estadístico=2.7077, p-valor (2 colas)=0.0225\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 20 — Respuesta\n","# (a) Chi-cuadrado de varianza — una muestra\n","np.random.seed(1234)\n","n_v = 20\n","mu_v, sigma_v = 10, 2\n","xv = np.random.randn(n_v) * sigma_v + mu_v\n","ssq = xv.var(ddof=1)\n","sigma0sq = 2 ** 2\n","\n","test_stat_chi2 = (n_v - 1) * ssq / sigma0sq\n","p_two_tail = 2 * min(1 - st.chi2.cdf(test_stat_chi2, n_v - 1), st.chi2.cdf(test_stat_chi2, n_v - 1))\n","print(f\"(a) Chi2 test: estadístico={test_stat_chi2:.4f}, p-valor (2 colas)={p_two_tail:.4f}\")\n","\n","# (b) F test — razón de varianzas entre dos muestras\n","n_a, n_b = 25, 20\n","xa = np.random.randn(n_a) * 2 + 10\n","xb = np.random.randn(n_b) * 4 - 5\n","ssq_a, ssq_b = xa.var(ddof=1), xb.var(ddof=1)\n","\n","test_stat_f = max(ssq_a, ssq_b) / min(ssq_a, ssq_b)\n","dfn, dfd = (n_b - 1, n_a - 1) if ssq_b > ssq_a else (n_a - 1, n_b - 1)\n","p_f = 2 * (1 - st.f.cdf(test_stat_f, dfn, dfd))\n","print(f\"(b) F test: estadístico={test_stat_f:.4f}, p-valor (2 colas)={p_f:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5c8dc83c","metadata":{"id":"5c8dc83c"},"source":["## Apartado 5 · Variables categóricas y test Chi-cuadrado (Ejercicios 21–25)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0175506f","metadata":{"id":"0175506f"},"source":["### Ejercicio 21\n","Sobre el dataset de estudiantes, construir la tabla de frecuencias (una vía) de `bloodtype` y de `gender`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"416a7db8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.573251Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.572723Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.578439Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.577731Z"},"id":"416a7db8","outputId":"b2a63ae4-189f-40f8-cabe-908544a50f52"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Frecuencias bloodtype:\n"," bloodtype\n","O     5\n","B     5\n","A     4\n","AB    3\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n","\n","Frecuencias gender:\n"," gender\n","M    10\n","F     7\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 21 — Respuesta\n","bloodType = df['bloodtype']\n","gender = df['gender']\n","\n","print(\"Frecuencias bloodtype:\\n\", bloodType.value_counts())\n","print(\"\\nFrecuencias gender:\\n\", gender.value_counts())\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5964291c","metadata":{"id":"5964291c"},"source":["### Ejercicio 22\n","Construir la tabla de proporciones (frecuencias relativas) de `bloodtype` y `gender`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"cdd5df08","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.580273Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.579711Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.585780Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.584992Z"},"id":"cdd5df08","outputId":"6dc85657-8640-483f-c900-4df28ac34793"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Proporciones bloodtype:\n"," bloodtype\n","O     0.294118\n","B     0.294118\n","A     0.235294\n","AB    0.176471\n","Name: count, dtype: float64\n","\n","Proporciones gender:\n"," gender\n","M    0.588235\n","F    0.411765\n","Name: count, dtype: float64\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 22 — Respuesta\n","prop_blood = bloodType.value_counts() / bloodType.size\n","prop_gender = gender.value_counts() / gender.size\n","\n","print(\"Proporciones bloodtype:\\n\", prop_blood)\n","print(\"\\nProporciones gender:\\n\", prop_gender)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d2f52c45","metadata":{"id":"d2f52c45"},"source":["### Ejercicio 23\n","Construir la tabla de contingencia (dos vías) entre `bloodtype` y `gender`, con y sin marginalización, y aplicar el test Chi-cuadrado de independencia."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"b6dbcc1b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.587610Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.587067Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.611282Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.610558Z"},"id":"b6dbcc1b","outputId":"277f9cbb-49a0-4675-b06c-d9ce49fdd451"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["gender     F  M\n","bloodtype      \n","A          2  2\n","AB         1  2\n","B          1  4\n","O          3  2\n","\n","gender     F   M  All\n","bloodtype            \n","A          2   2    4\n","AB         1   2    3\n","B          1   4    5\n","O          3   2    5\n","All        7  10   17\n","\n","Chi2 = 1.8619,  p-valor = 0.6016,  df = 3\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 23 — Respuesta\n","tabla = pd.crosstab(bloodType, gender)\n","tabla_margin = pd.crosstab(bloodType, gender, margins=True)\n","print(tabla)\n","print()\n","print(tabla_margin)\n","\n","chi2, p, dof, expected = st.chi2_contingency(tabla)\n","print(f\"\\nChi2 = {chi2:.4f},  p-valor = {p:.4f},  df = {dof}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ac884078","metadata":{"id":"ac884078"},"source":["### Ejercicio 24\n","Con la tabla de frecuencias del color de ojos de 592 adultos, aplicar el test Chi-cuadrado de bondad de ajuste comparando contra (a) el modelo de frecuencias iguales y (b) un modelo teórico más realista (40%, 33%, 15%, 12%)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"6681d6d3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.613052Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.612456Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.618433Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.617774Z"},"id":"6681d6d3","outputId":"7be9a1b8-e47f-4bba-c993-25674d2422d2"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["(a) Modelo frecuencias iguales: Power_divergenceResult(statistic=np.float64(133.47297297297297), pvalue=np.float64(9.650879774148268e-29))\n","(b) Modelo realista (40/33/15/12%): Power_divergenceResult(statistic=np.float64(4.06265356265356), pvalue=np.float64(0.25477767063672113))\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 24 — Respuesta\n","data_eye = np.array([220, 215, 93, 64])\n","eye = pd.Series(data_eye, index=['Brown', 'Blue', 'Hazel', 'Green'])\n","\n","# (a) Modelo de frecuencias iguales\n","res_igual = st.chisquare(eye)\n","print(\"(a) Modelo frecuencias iguales:\", res_igual)\n","\n","# (b) Modelo teórico realista\n","my_model = eye.sum() * np.array([0.40, 0.33, 0.15, 0.12])\n","res_realista = st.chisquare(f_obs=eye, f_exp=my_model)\n","print(\"(b) Modelo realista (40/33/15/12%):\", res_realista)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"06206298","metadata":{"id":"06206298"},"source":["### Ejercicio 25\n","Con la tabla de contingencia del RMS Titanic (clase del camarote vs. supervivencia), aplicar el test Chi-cuadrado de independencia y concluir si ambas variables son independientes."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"b76a3238","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.619855Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.619708Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.626431Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.625743Z"},"id":"b76a3238","outputId":"0405ee01-7ae5-4c38-9ccc-2e4c1a8254b3"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["      Yes   No\n","1st   122  203\n","2nd   167  118\n","3rd   528  178\n","Crew  673  212\n","\n","Chi2 = 190.4011,  p-valor = 0.000000,  df = 3\n","Se rechaza independencia: clase y supervivencia están asociadas.\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 25 — Respuesta\n","data_survived = {'Yes': [122, 167, 528, 673], 'No': [203, 118, 178, 212]}\n","titanic = pd.DataFrame(data_survived, index=['1st', '2nd', '3rd', 'Crew'])\n","print(titanic)\n","\n","chi2_t, p_t, dof_t, expected_t = st.chi2_contingency(titanic)\n","print(f\"\\nChi2 = {chi2_t:.4f},  p-valor = {p_t:.6f},  df = {dof_t}\")\n","\n","conclusion = \"Se rechaza independencia: clase y supervivencia están asociadas.\" if p_t < 0.05 \\\n","    else \"No se rechaza independencia.\"\n","print(conclusion)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"aae42cf8","metadata":{"id":"aae42cf8"},"source":["## Apartado 6 · Regresión y Machine Learning con scikit-learn (Ejercicios 26–30)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f8814b85","metadata":{"id":"f8814b85"},"source":["### Ejercicio 26\n","Ajustar una regresión lineal simple con `scikit-learn` para predecir `height` a partir de `weight` en el dataset de estudiantes. Reportar el coeficiente, el intercepto, el R² y graficar la recta ajustada sobre el scatter."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"97ab8e72","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.628223Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.627658Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.782510Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.781541Z"},"id":"97ab8e72","outputId":"d4453295-e3c0-4a0f-fec9-86714834c6b3"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Coeficiente (pendiente) = 0.4399\n","Intercepto              = 143.1724\n","R²                      = 0.4411\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 26 — Respuesta\n","X = df[['weight']].values\n","y = df['height'].values\n","\n","lin_reg = LinearRegression()\n","lin_reg.fit(X, y)\n","y_pred = lin_reg.predict(X)\n","\n","print(f\"Coeficiente (pendiente) = {lin_reg.coef_[0]:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Intercepto              = {lin_reg.intercept_:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"R²                      = {r2_score(y, y_pred):.4f}\")\n","\n","plt.scatter(X, y, alpha=0.7, label='Datos')\n","plt.plot(X, y_pred, color='red', lw=2, label='Regresión lineal')\n","plt.xlabel('weight')\n","plt.ylabel('height')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.title('Regresión lineal simple: height ~ weight')\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5e79490c","metadata":{"id":"5e79490c"},"source":["### Ejercicio 27\n","Usando el dataset Iris, ajustar una regresión lineal múltiple para predecir `Sepal.Length` a partir de `Sepal.Width`, `Petal.Length` y `Petal.Width`, separando en entrenamiento/prueba (80/20) y reportando RMSE y R² en el conjunto de prueba."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"caa84667","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.784455Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.783909Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.791964Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.791167Z"},"id":"caa84667","outputId":"393c61fe-5b4a-42fd-c5b9-9cfc3a56c4e0"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Coeficientes: {'Sepal.Width': np.float64(0.6682327909412715), 'Petal.Length': np.float64(0.7599077535500263), 'Petal.Width': np.float64(-0.681946575958206)}\n","Intercepto = 1.7399\n","RMSE (test) = 0.3197\n","R²   (test) = 0.8519\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 27 — Respuesta\n","X_iris = df_iris[['Sepal.Width', 'Petal.Length', 'Petal.Width']].values\n","y_iris = df_iris['Sepal.Length'].values\n","\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X_iris, y_iris, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n","\n","reg_multi = LinearRegression()\n","reg_multi.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","y_pred_multi = reg_multi.predict(X_test)\n","\n","rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred_multi))\n","r2 = r2_score(y_test, y_pred_multi)\n","\n","print(\"Coeficientes:\", dict(zip(['Sepal.Width', 'Petal.Length', 'Petal.Width'], reg_multi.coef_)))\n","print(f\"Intercepto = {reg_multi.intercept_:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"RMSE (test) = {rmse:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"R²   (test) = {r2:.4f}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5929d1cd","metadata":{"id":"5929d1cd"},"source":["### Ejercicio 28\n","Entrenar un clasificador K-Nearest Neighbors (K=5) para predecir `Species` en el dataset Iris a partir de sus 4 variables numéricas, con estandarización previa (`StandardScaler`), y reportar la exactitud (`accuracy`) y la matriz de confusión sobre el conjunto de prueba."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"50b36008","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.793272Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.793140Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.804702Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.804042Z"},"id":"50b36008","outputId":"98d136f8-a1ba-4879-8e17-44cc571c34f5"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Accuracy = 0.9211\n","Matriz de confusión:\n","            setosa  versicolor  virginica\n","setosa          12           0          0\n","versicolor       0          13          0\n","virginica        0           3         10\n"]}],"source":["# Ejercicio 28 — Respuesta\n","X_feat = df_iris[['Sepal.Length', 'Sepal.Width', 'Petal.Length', 'Petal.Width']].values\n","y_species = df_iris['Species'].values\n","\n","X_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X_feat, y_species, test_size=0.25, random_state=42, stratify=y_species)\n","\n","scaler = StandardScaler()\n","X_tr_s = scaler.fit_transform(X_tr)\n","X_te_s = scaler.transform(X_te)\n","\n","knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=5)\n","knn.fit(X_tr_s, y_tr)\n","y_pred_knn = knn.predict(X_te_s)\n","\n","acc = accuracy_score(y_te, y_pred_knn)\n","cm = confusion_matrix(y_te, y_pred_knn, labels=np.unique(y_species))\n","\n","print(f\"Accuracy = {acc:.4f}\")\n","print(\"Matriz de confusión:\")\n","print(pd.DataFrame(cm, index=np.unique(y_species), columns=np.unique(y_species)))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1c648cd6","metadata":{"id":"1c648cd6"},"source":["### Ejercicio 29\n","Aplicar un Análisis de Componentes Principales (PCA) a las 4 variables numéricas del Iris, reducir a 2 componentes, reportar la varianza explicada por cada uno y graficar la proyección coloreada por especie."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"e4d75ed6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.806055Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.805923Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.901767Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-22T00:55:35.901032Z"},"id":"e4d75ed6","outputId":"c6d49725-594a-4e48-9ef6-0eeb82a0defb"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Varianza explicada por componente: [0.72770452 0.23030523]\n","Varianza explicada acumulada: 0.9580097536148195\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Ejercicio 29 — Respuesta\n","X_pca_in = StandardScaler().fit_transform(X_feat)\n","\n","pca = PCA(n_components=2)\n","X_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_pca_in)\n","\n","print(\"Varianza explicada por componente:\", pca.explained_variance_ratio_)\n","print(\"Varianza explicada acumulada:\", pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum())\n","\n","plt.figure()\n","for especie in np.unique(y_species):\n","    mask = y_species == especie\n","    plt.scatter(X_pca[mask, 0], X_pca[mask, 1], label=especie, alpha=0.7)\n","plt.xlabel('PC1')\n","plt.ylabel('PC2')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.title('PCA del dataset Iris (2 componentes)')\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"36ca363e","metadata":{"id":"36ca363e"},"source":["### Ejercicio 30\n","Comparar mediante validación cruzada (5-fold `cross_val_score`) el desempeño de dos clasificadores — Regresión Logística y Árbol de Decisión — sobre el dataset Iris, reportando la exactitu